# One region filter for Guided learning

The main catalogue uses one native GET form for search, view and region. Its
region allowlist is the existing Atlas navigation list, not a new anatomy
mapping. Selecting a region applies to the regional 3D results and the linked
head catalogue together. Head CT/MRI sequences appear only for All regions or
Head & neck. Other regions in CT/MRI show an explicit unavailable state, with
separate choices to browse that region's 3D tours or head imaging tours.

Search, view changes and Clear search retain the selected region in the URL.
Browser Back/Forward therefore restores the full catalogue filter. A regional
search opens its results in All tours/3D; CT/MRI never auto-expand 3D controls.
Embedded regional results suppress their duplicate search/region controls.
Other uses of the regional component keep their original interactive defaults.
No matching tours means zero results, not a fallback to another region.

These are discovery controls. They do not start tours, open scans, store scores,
grant access, add mappings or approve content. Existing canonical tour links,
source revisions, draft notices, independent entitlements and approval gates
are unchanged. Regional 3D surfaces and CT/MRI remain separate subjects unless
independently validated; this is not spatial synchronization.

The isolated candidate has native page/parser/component tests, an actual
production build, and a 1280×720 browser check of native GET navigation using
synthetic catalogue metadata. That fixture is server-rendered, not a hydrated
or authenticated Website session, and loads no patient study or 3D model.
Strict configured checks cover the actual changed parser and regional controls.
The full actual page's larger import graph failed at 256 and 384 MiB heap limits;
that semantic type check remains resource-gated, not passed or replaced by the
focused scope. Whole-project, authenticated and clinical acceptance remain open.

The owner's normal local preview is unchanged. All browser evidence and failed
resource checks stay on F drive; only selected authored source is eligible for
the separate verified GitHub source backup.
